        "original_id": "557f3378-8002-58a4-88b2-60a27eb97851",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Duluth Ship Canal, Cross Florida Barge Canal\n- Places: Florida, Gulf of Mexico, Atlantic Ocean\n- Concepts: federal supervision, environmental opposition, greenway\n\nFacts:\n- The Duluth Ship Canal was begun privately in 1871.\n- The Duluth Ship Canal was put under federal supervision and maintenance several years after it began.\n- The Cross Florida Barge Canal was a canal project intended to connect the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean across Florida for barge traffic.\n- Opposition to the Cross Florida Barge Canal was led by Marjorie Harris Carr.\n- Two sections of the Cross Florida Barge Canal were built before the project was cancelled mainly for environmental reasons.\n- The former Cross Florida Barge Canal corridor is now officially the Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway, a protected green belt corridor that is one mile wide in most places.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0ddfe42b-3913-5d47-936e-2da160e200c6",
        "text": "Page: Duluth Ship Canal. Sentence: Begun privately in 1871, it was put under federal supervision and maintenance several years later.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: The Cross Florida Barge Canal, now officially the Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway is a protected green belt corridor, one mile (1.6 km) wide in most places.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: It is named for the leader of opposition to the Cross Florida Barge Canal, a canal project to connect the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean across Florida for barge traffic.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: Two sections were built but the project was cancelled, mainly for environmental reasons.",
